{# The header's notifications link and its unread count.

   Its own template with its own id because every notification action changes
   the number in it: marking one read, marking all read, deleting an unread
   one. Those handlers answer with an `<hx-partial>` pointed here, so the count
   is corrected by the same request that caused it to change. Before this it
   was only ever right on a fresh page load, and sat there overstating the
   unread count for the rest of the visit. #}
{%- set unread_count = unread_notification_count if unread_notification_count is defined else 0 %}
{# data-unread is the count the apps are sent (app_bridge.jinja). #}
<span id="nav-notifications" data-unread="{{ unread_count }}">
  {# A bell, beside search's magnifier: the two icons at the bar's end, the
     rest of it words. It was a word while every other button was one too,
     and a bell among them the one control to decode; search became an icon
     for width, and this follows it for the same reason.

     Unread shows as the bell itself, filled in and in the badge's orange,
     rather than as a count beside it or on its corner: the button is one
     width at 0 unread or 99, so the count never decides whether the bar
     fits on one row -- the thing drafts were taken out of the bar to stop.
     Filled as well as coloured, so it is not colour alone that says so. The
     number is still in the label and the tooltip. #}
  {%- set unread = unread_notification_count is defined and unread_notification_count > 0 %}
  {%- set label = ftl_get_message("notifications") ~ (" (" ~ unread_notification_count ~ ")" if unread else "") %}
  <a href="/notifications" class="toolbar-square toolbar-button toolbar-bell{% if unread %} toolbar-bell-unread{% endif %}"
     aria-label="{{ label }}" title="{{ label }}">
    <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 16.5v-5.5a6 6 0 0 1 12 0v5.5l1.5 2h-15z"/><path d="M10 21.5h4"/></svg>
  </a>
</span>
